[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2667014305","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103014#issuecomment-2667014305","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103014","id":2667014305,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6e92ih","user":{"login":"stuartcarnie","id":52852,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyODUy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52852?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie","html_url":"https://github.com/stuartcarnie","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-18T21:57:18Z","updated_at":"2025-02-18T21:57:18Z","body":"@Calinou it is possible for me to get total GPU time; just not per viewport. Is there a way we could make this work?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2667014305/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2667024876","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103014#issuecomment-2667024876","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103014","id":2667024876,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6e95Hs","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-18T22:03:23Z","updated_at":"2025-02-18T22:03:23Z","body":"> @Calinou it is possible for me to get total GPU time; just not per viewport. Is there a way we could make this work?\r\n\r\nThere is no RenderingServer method exposed to query the total GPU time, only GPU time per viewport. I suppose new methods would need to be exposed for that (also for the CPU if relevant).\r\n\r\nAlso, do you still get granularity on the subsections of the GPU time if you get a total value? For example, how much GPU time was spent rendering directional shadows, SSAO and so on.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2667024876/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2667309308","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103014#issuecomment-2667309308","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103014","id":2667309308,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6e--j8","user":{"login":"stuartcarnie","id":52852,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyODUy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52852?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie","html_url":"https://github.com/stuartcarnie","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-19T01:40:18Z","updated_at":"2025-02-19T01:40:18Z","body":"> Also, do you still get granularity on the subsections of the GPU time if you get a total value? For example, how much GPU time was spent rendering directional shadows, SSAO and so on.\r\n\r\nThe total value is how long the GPU took to execute the last batch of submitted commands, which is all subsections.\r\n\r\nThere isn't an easy way to do this with the current profiling architecture, which expects the driver to generate timestamps as each subset of commands is executed, and then subtract the previous from the next to determine the total time. Metal, and probably other TBDR GPUs, can reorder commands based on dependencies, to improve parallelisation. The only way it might be possible with the current architecture is to insert artificial fences / events, which defeats the purpose.\r\n\r\nPerhaps we could defer profiling to the `RenderingDeviceDriver`, it might be doable. Metal has support for capturing timestamps at the start and end of a draw or compute dispatch, and then we can determine the total time the pass took.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2667309308/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2676145679","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103014#issuecomment-2676145679","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103014","id":2676145679,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6fgr4P","user":{"login":"hishnash","id":838127,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzODEyNw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/838127?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hishnash","html_url":"https://github.com/hishnash","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hishnash/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hishnash/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hishnash/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hishnash/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hishnash/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hishnash/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hishnash/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hishnash/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hishnash/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-22T10:54:01Z","updated_at":"2025-02-22T10:54:01Z","body":"You might be able to do this using the new metal debug shader messages https://developer.apple.com/documentation/metal/logging-shader-debug-messages since you can emit these at any point within any shadier and I believe the time stamp they get is when they are called.  ","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2676145679/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2676361786","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103014#issuecomment-2676361786","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103014","id":2676361786,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6fhgo6","user":{"login":"stuartcarnie","id":52852,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyODUy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52852?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie","html_url":"https://github.com/stuartcarnie","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-22T19:25:29Z","updated_at":"2025-02-22T19:25:29Z","body":"@hishnash it's an interesting feature, for sure, and I was excited to learn about it at the last WWDC, but it only works on iOS 18+, macOS 15+, etc. Further, I'm not even sure we would be able to execute the log messages only once on the first and last invocation of a shader to capture the start and end times[^1]. \r\n\r\n[^1]: We need to add a log for the first and last invocation, as the GPU can reorder commands.\r\n\r\nShaders execute the entry-point function multiple times, so we'd need to know how to execute the log message on the first call and last call only and then modify the generated source to inject that into the shader. On top of that, we then need to specify additional environment variables and change compiler settings to enable log support. Then we need to read the log stream to locate the message and parse them out. ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2676361786/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2774867702","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103014#issuecomment-2774867702","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103014","id":2774867702,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6lZR72","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-03T08:24:16Z","updated_at":"2025-04-03T08:24:16Z","body":"We should resolve this sooner than later, as the current state is confusing for users.\r\n\r\nShould we go with this for now as a stopgap solution until property GPU render time profiling is implemented for Metal one way or another?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2774867702/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2775685122","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103014#issuecomment-2775685122","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103014","id":2775685122,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6lcZgC","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-03T12:48:53Z","updated_at":"2025-04-03T12:50:13Z","body":"> Should we go with this for now as a stopgap solution until property GPU render time profiling is implemented for Metal one way or another?\r\n\r\nI think it's better to merge this now, considering Metal GPU profiling will not be cherry-picked to 4.4.x (while this PR can).\r\n\r\nNote that the editor FPS display is handled in https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99301 instead.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2775685122/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]